    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "A binary operation is defined by a o b = a/b. Find 2 o 5."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Think first: The left input goes on top of the fraction and the right input goes underneath."
    },
    {
      "type": "asset",
      "storagePath": "assets/question_visuals/p057_q08.jpg",
      "altText": "Source visual for edmar-csec-p057-q08 from workbook page 57."
    }
  ],
  "solutionSteps": [
    {
      "stepNo": 1,
      "instruction": "Substitute a = 2 and b = 5.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: 2/5"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "stepNo": 2,
      "instruction": "Give the decimal equivalent if required.",
      "contentBlocks": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "2 divided by 5"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "value": "Result: 0.4"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "strategyBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Substitute a = 2 and b = 5 into a/b."
    }
  ],
  "finalAnswerBlocks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "2 o 5 = 2/5, that is 0.4"
    }
  ],
  "whyThisWorks": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "Division is not commutative, so the order of the inputs completely changes the answer: 2 o 5 is 0.4 while 5 o 2 is 2.5. Leaving the answer as the fraction 2/5 is exact, and the decimal 0.4 is simply another way of writing it."
    }
  ],
